be far more disrupted than their counterparts in the higher speed VRS. The simulations presented in this paper were of a single-bladed rotor that trailed tip and root vortices of constant and equal strength into the flow field. In addition, the blade aerodynamics was uncoupled from the velocity field. It is possible that such simplifications could influence the generality of the findings of this work. The wake of a multibladed rotor operating under the same flight conditions may well comprise a number of coherent ring-like vortex structures different from that of the
